<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-246 amendment, Sam's ruling of 2026-11-21 (T2 nexus/sam-ruling-split-move-bounds-2026-11-21, which amends decision C of
    nexus/sam-ruling-rdr229-ask-c-2026-11-21): the finisher's verification gets a statement timeout of its own.

    nexus.data_moves.statement_timeout_ms bounded both the verification and the completion transaction. The completion
    transaction (the completed_at UPDATE and on_complete) holds locks, so its bound has to be short (decision C: 1400 ms
    statement, 700 ms lock). A verification read on a cold, freshly stamped table can need far longer than that (P3.2 measured
    the chunk-key swap's foreign key check at about 13 s on the cloud disk), and it takes ACCESS SHARE only, so it can wait.

    Column:
      verify_statement_timeout_ms  the bound on the finisher's first, READ ONLY verification pass (per tenant and table-wide);
                                   positive. That pass is also the warm-up: a plain scan, no pg_prewarm. The completion
                                   transaction runs the verification again under statement_timeout_ms, now warm, before it
                                   writes completed_at. NOT NULL DEFAULT 60000, so every registered move (a registering INSERT
                                   names no such column) takes 60 s.

    One ALTER TABLE statement, so the CHECK is added with the column. DDL only: the default fills the existing rows without a
    rewrite (a constant default), and no row DML is written. Rollback drops the column, which drops its CHECK.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="datamoves-002-1" author="rdr246-split-move-bounds">
        <comment>nexus.data_moves.verify_statement_timeout_ms: the finisher's READ ONLY verification pass gets its own bound (default 60000 ms)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.data_moves
    ADD COLUMN verify_statement_timeout_ms INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 60000
    CONSTRAINT data_moves_verify_statement_timeout_ms_check CHECK (verify_statement_timeout_ms &gt; 0);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            ALTER TABLE nexus.data_moves DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS verify_statement_timeout_ms;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
